      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason is that we change the flush_tlb callback at runtime: https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/kernel/common/+/3672457/16/arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/mmu.c#199\n\nBut actually we discussed that with Chuanxiao and Kevin during v6.15 review, for example here: https://github.com/intel-staging/pKVM-IA/pull/40#discussion_r2315634205 (in the context of improving the pgtable API to enforce using const pointers for these ops), and concluded that it\u0027s not a big problem to do that differently and avoid changing flush_tlb at runtime and thus avoid this per-VM copy. Maybe I\u0027ll already do that in this series.\n\npKVM-ARM also has this per-VM copy of mm_ops, I\u0027m not sure what for.",
      "parentUuid": "7f09d161_10dbc040",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
