      "writtenOn": "2025-09-22T16:02:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not related to this change, but I am a bit confused here. Should we be calling `pkvm_vm_destroy` here? I feel `free_pkvm_vm_handle` will not be called in case of failure as vmx_vm_destroy doesn\u0027t do that. `pkvm_vm_destroy` would basically cleanup everything that is partially setup in this function and seems the logical thing to do. What do you think?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 193,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "967b052e_6609cd32",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 190,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 190,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "// The cleanup labels below handle failures at different stages of pkvm_vm_init.\n// pkvm_vm_destroy is not used in these failure paths because it assumes a\n// fully initialized VM, including a successfully allocated handle. Since\n// failures can occur before allocate_pkvm_vm_handle(), the current structure\n// ensures that only resources that were successfully set up are properly torn down.\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "3e78ac09b7c7a8fed03acd7d62ecbfcbb3142c40",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "771af41d_46f0b683",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 193,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-22T20:32:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I feel `free_pkvm_vm_handle` will not be called in case of failure as vmx_vm_destroy doesn\u0027t do that.\n\nIt doesn\u0027t look like we should call `free_pkvm_vm_handle()` here. `allocate_pkvm_vm_handle()` has failed to allocate a VM handle, so no need to free it, and we don\u0027t even have a VM handle to pass to `free_pkvm_vm_handle()` (or to `pkvm_vm_destroy()` for that matter), right?\n\nAlthough while we\u0027re at it, since we\u0027ve called `kvm_arch_init_vm()`, it seems it would be cleaner to call `kvm_arch_destroy_vm()` here instead of `kvm_x86_call(vm_destroy)()` (even though currently they do the same). @chuanxiao.dong@intel.corp-partner.google.com for visibility.",
      "parentUuid": "e51ee6db_28b7cf37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 193,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3e78ac09b7c7a8fed03acd7d62ecbfcbb3142c40",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76ade991_8956290a",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
