      "writtenOn": "2025-09-23T00:41:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes youre right, I didn\u0027t realize `pkvm_vm_destroy()` takes handle to do cleanup. Ideally I envisioned `pkvm_vm_destroy` to the exact wind down of this function so that we need not call cleanup of each init logic on failure(like mmu_destroy, followed by arch_destroy_vm followed by undonate pages). Instead of cleaning up each of these with multiple gotos, a single call to `pkvm_vm_destroy` logic on error which cleans up each of the above based on whether it was initialized or not. Its doable, but looks like its needs a rewrite of `pkvm_vm_destroy()` and is not in the scope of this patch. So as you suggested, lets handle `kvm_arch_destroy_vm` which is the only one left out in the current logic",
      "parentUuid": "771af41d_46f0b683",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 193,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3e78ac09b7c7a8fed03acd7d62ecbfcbb3142c40",
