      "side": 1,
      "message": "`vmx_vm_destroy` defined in `arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/vmx/vmx.c` does not call `kvm_arch_destroy_vm()` as far as I can see.\n```\nvoid vmx_vm_destroy(struct kvm *kvm)\n{\n#ifdef __PKVM_HYP__\n       /*\n        * FIXME: Teardown shadow vm as it is initialized when doing\n        * vm init. Should revisit when PV method is ready.\n        */\n       pkvm_teardown_shadow_vm(kvm);\n\n       /*\n        * TODO: Support teardown the pid_table in the pkvm hypervisor when ipiv\n        * is supported.\n        */\n#else\n       struct kvm_vmx *kvm_vmx \u003d to_kvm_vmx(kvm);\n\n       free_pages((unsigned long)kvm_vmx-\u003epid_table, vmx_get_pid_table_order(kvm));\n#endif\n}\n```\n\nNot sure if I am looking at the wrong place?",
